        "original_id": "f4f81a7d-ba5d-57e2-b586-58ed10011d90",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Lancaster, Lancashire, England, Peel, Isle of Man\n- Organizations: Lancaster Cathedral, Peel Cathedral\n- Concepts: Roman Catholic parish church, cathedral status, parish churches, rebranding\n\nFacts:\n- Peel Cathedral, formally the Cathedral Church of Saint German, was built in Peel on the Isle of Man from 1879 to 1884.\n- Lancaster Cathedral is also known as The Cathedral Church of St Peter and Saint Peter's Cathedral, and it is on St Peter's Road in Lancaster, Lancashire, England.\n- In 1924, Lancaster Cathedral was elevated from a Roman Catholic parish church to cathedral status.\n- Peel Cathedral was rebranded as Cathedral Isle of Man.\n- Peel Cathedral is one of the parish churches in the parish of the West Coast, which includes the town of Peel.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "13bb74b6-45d8-5688-ac83-357349f6e91c",
        "text": "Page: Lancaster Cathedral. Sentence: Lancaster Cathedral, also known as The Cathedral Church of St Peter and Saint Peter's Cathedral, is in St Peter's Road, Lancaster, Lancashire, England.\nPage: Lancaster Cathedral. Sentence: It was a Roman Catholic parish church until 1924, when it was elevated to the status of a cathedral.\nPage: Peel Cathedral. Sentence: The Cathedral Church of Saint German or Peel Cathedral, rebranded as Cathedral Isle of Man is located in Peel, Isle of Man.\nPage: Peel Cathedral. Sentence: The cathedral is also one of the parish churches in the parish of the West Coast which includes the town of Peel, and was built in 1879–84.",
